{"base_rate":0.256797583081571,"brier":0.13860966767371602,"bss":0.27373439502630326,"bss_hi":0.3749978993157886,"bss_lo":0.15201546831387927,"chart":{"base":[395.0,62.5],"fp":[320.5,372.9],"lead":"62,237.3 272,226 482,201.1 692,173.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.27 — higher than 44% of cities","fp":"low end +12pp, high end -1pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 34% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 11%; promised 69% → rained 70%"},"rel":"62,417.2 129.6,372.3 497.1,163.9"},"country":"DZ","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09108761329305136,"ess":312.5613277013021,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Oran</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Oran rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (88%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>11%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 662 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 8.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 119 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(65&ndash;161) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>363</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>99</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>49%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Oran</b> <span class=\"muted\">Algeria</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>65&ndash;161\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>662 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Oran &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Oran\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.019504132231404,380.9972451790634 75.12787878787879,348.9090909090909 126.84507462686567,278.77611940298505 228.98761904761903,162.44444444444446 368.6602857142857,38.80000000000001 368.6602857142857,90.80000000000001 228.98761904761903,249.11111111111111 126.84507462686567,343.97014925373134 75.12787878787879,378.32323232323233 58.019504132231404,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"288.5256797583081\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"288.5256797583081\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.019504132231404,340.8870523415978 75.12787878787879,337.8787878787879 126.84507462686567,251.61194029850748 228.98761904761903,202.88888888888889 368.6602857142857,59.60000000000002\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 363 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.019504132231404\" cy=\"340.8870523415978\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 99 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"75.12787878787879\" cy=\"337.8787878787879\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"126.84507462686567\" cy=\"251.61194029850748\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 48%&amp;#10;It rained 49% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"228.98761904761903\" cy=\"202.88888888888889\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"368.6602857142857\" cy=\"59.60000000000002\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(26%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Oran the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.32) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.03).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>168</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>-0.035</td><td class='num'>21.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>140</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.229</td><td class='num'>7.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>158</td><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'>0.310</td><td class='num'>0.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>196</td><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'>0.320</td><td class='num'>7.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":35.69906,"lon":-0.63588,"n":662,"n_cities":213,"name":"Oran","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":5.509641873278237e-05,"n":363,"obs":0.11294765840220386,"sig":true},{"hi":0.13,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.04838383838383838,"n":99,"obs":0.12121212121212122,"sig":true},{"hi":0.32400000000000206,"lo":0.13,"mean":0.1944776119402985,"n":67,"obs":0.3582089552238806,"sig":true},{"hi":0.7,"lo":0.32400000000000206,"mean":0.48301587301587295,"n":63,"obs":0.49206349206349204,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.7,"mean":0.8775714285714286,"n":70,"obs":0.8857142857142857,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":8.5,"provisional":false,"rank":119,"rank_hi":161.02499999999998,"rank_lo":65.0,"reliability":0.010509608031003067,"resolution":0.062228216342591916,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"oran","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Algie